/* ============================================================================
   Quest journal - generated by tools/foundryExport/quest_journal.py
   Builds the quest's journals in one JournalEntry folder, one page per scene,
   place or NPC. A journal of the same name in that folder is REPLACED, so the
   repo stays the source of truth: edit the GM pages, regenerate, re-run.
   Journals are GM-only; show an image page to the table with "Show Players".
   ========================================================================== */
(async () => {
  if (!game.user.isGM) return ui.notifications.error("Run this macro as the GM.");
  const SPEC = {"folder": "The Unspent", "journals": [{"name": "The Unspent · Chapter 1: Struck Colours", "pages": [{"name": "1 · The Goodmeasure", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Calm, then fight · the opening</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Ship: the Goodmeasure, a small luxury stillship of the Solkai crossing · Master Ozhra · the crew · Redsail</p>\n<h3>Beat 1 · Where you are, and why</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>The posting on the Guild board in Merkavar had been boring. Boring but profitable. A merchant, some precious cargo and a need for some weapons, ideally attached to people that knew how to use them.</p><p>A simple guarding job: make sure that the cargo reaches Solkai, preferably in full.</p><p>You took it, the clerk stamped it and half a day later you were on a ship. Drifting across the lake at Merkavar watching Helgafjall shrink behind you. Not literally, or so you hoped.</p><p>Down the river you went and then the ship was dumped into the Midarra.</p><p>And you'd been here ever since, moving for nine days, still Midarra. The most exciting things were other ships that were drifting by close enough that the next round of I spy at least had something to go on other than blue.</p><p>Maybe it was time again. The time of day to open the crate for the 17th time and check that indeed yes, the Lautaran silk had stayed Lautaran silk.</p><p>Maybe it was time to get Master Ozhra to open one of his precious bottles of Catjomin sake, 4pm was a reasonable time after all.</p><p>Maybe it was finally time to break into the locked cabin and see the dark and twisted objects of secrecy Master Ozhra had kept for himself. Because surely he must be a cult worshiper and hidden behind there must be a corrupted crystal turning the minds of mortals into mush. Surely he hired you so you could serve as his next victims.</p><p>After all the alternative was a worse fate. You were just normal guards stuck on a merchant ship.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Why they are aboard</h4><p>The party are the ship's hired muscle, taken on through the Guild at Merkavar on short notice. A crew of their level is not cheap; the cargo is worth it. Ozhra carries luxury goods north to Solkai: Eldaran almosts, Emarrean sake, Lautaran silk.</p><p>He bought no Lord's colours for the crossing, on purpose. Colours are worth only as much as a Lord's name, and the raid the tellers love best is the one that breaks another Lord's colours; so on this run Ozhra trusts steel over pennants. He is in the middle of the crossing, in water the Lords share out, flying no one's colours, and that is why the ship is fair prize.</p>\n<section class=\"secret\"><p><strong>⚿ GM Secret · What is in the locked cabin</strong></p>\n<p><b>An eight-stripe Catjomin Sake</b> (<i>Uraharagiri</i>, Mist of the Hidden Meadow): a Hidden Treasure from a kitsune sacred vault, opened only by ancestral rite. It should never have left Emarrea. Anyone who knows Catjomin recognises the tier at a glance, and the stripes are never spoken aloud.</p>\n<p><b>Temple-stamped dream-blends</b> from the Dreaming Cape: genuine tier-four brews, the Twin Lantern's mark on every flask, made to promote vivid restful dreaming. A stamped blend is only to be drunk under a chartered inn's roof; carrying it away breaks the temple's licence. Ozhra bought a case from an inn-keeper who said yes to an outside merchant, the Cape's own sore point, and Solkai's rich will pay well for a real Cape dream at home. A Religion or Society check (or anyone from Lautara) knows the flasks should never have left the inn.</p>\n<p>Either one would ruin Ozhra if found. They are also exactly the kind of prize a Pirate Lord's crew would love to tell about.</p>\n</section>\n<h3>Beat 2 · A moment to breathe</h3>\n<h4>Run it</h4><p>Let the players introduce their characters to each other and to the crew: a meal on deck, a game of dice on a grain sack, the evening watch. The crew run the ship; the party only guard it, and the crew are curious about them. Give each player a crew member to talk to.</p>\n<h4>Who's here · the crew</h4>\n<p>A crossing crew from Tvisol, as mixed as its ports. Full sheets on the cast page.</p>\n<ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Tarrek</b> · bosun, Minotaur: patient, misses his vines out loud</li><li><b>Shab</b> · purser, Kholo, Ozhra's niece: knows what he did not pay for</li><li><b>Hangas</b> · cook, Dragonet: feeds everyone too much, goes quiet about colours</li><li><b>Ankhes Khata</b> · deckhand, Duskwalker: wants every adventure story</li><li><b>Patala Latasi</b> · lookout, Goloma: calls the sail</li></ul>\n<h3>Beat 3 · Ozhra's question</h3>\n<h4>Run it</h4><p>While they talk, Master Ozhra walks the deck: up to the bow, back to the wheel, up to the bow again, looking at the horizon and not at the sails. At last he drifts over to the party, too casual.</p><p><i>\"You'd know a Lord's ship, would you? At a distance, I mean. Say, a mile off. Before it was close enough to matter.\"</i> If they ask why: <i>\"No reason. Good eyes are good to have. That's all.\"</i> Then the thanks, too warm and too long: he takes the nearest hand in both of his and holds on to it. <i>\"Thank you. Truly. I chose well with you, I knew it at the Guild, and I'll tell the clerk so myself when we're home. Have you eaten? Hangas will feed you. Go on, go on.\"</i></p><p>Then he is off again, bow to wheel. His claws click on the planks, quick and even. At the bow he stops, ears forward, and stares out over the water far longer than there is anything to see. On the way back he looks at the locked cabin door and away again. At the wheel he turns his back on the sea, and his hand finds the key on its chain at his throat.</p>\n<h4>◈ Reading Ozhra: Perception vs his Deception</h4>\nDC 32 · Ozhra: Level 2 in a fight, Non-Combat Level 10 as a merchant; Deception High (+22) · any player who heard him may roll · Shab can be pressed afterwards (Diplomacy DC 21)\n<b>Critical Success (≥42):</b> He bought no Lord's colours for this crossing, by choice, and he is carrying something in the locked cabin he must not be caught with. He is afraid of a Lord's ship more than of pirates.\n<b>Success (≥32):</b> He is hiding something about flags or colours. His question was about a Lord's ship specifically, and pirates in general do not worry him half as much.\n<b>Failure (&lt;32):</b> A careful master with a valuable cargo on a long crossing. Nothing more.\n<b>Critical Failure (≤22):</b> He convinces them all is in order, and on the way back to the wheel he pats the pennant locker as if colours were in it.\n<h4>Ozhra at the table</h4><p>Combat Level 2; Non-Combat Level 10 as an important merchant of the crossing. Deception +22 (DC 32), Diplomacy +22, Mercantile Lore +25. Will +22 (DC 32 to Coerce or Request), Perception +19 (DC 29 to lie to him). Fortitude +8, Reflex +5. Shab: Non-Combat Level 4 purser; Diplomacy against her is DC 21 (her level, +2 because she is loyal to him first).</p>\n<h3>Beat 4 · The lookout calls</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>\"Sail!\" Patala's voice comes down from the nest, high and certain. \"Sail off the port bow!\"</p><p>A lean two-master is coming out of the glare, flying a trader's pennant, the kind half the ships on the crossing fly. You hear a breath escape Ozhra and see his shoulders drop, before they seem to pull up again. Then the pennant comes down, hand over hand, and a flag runs up in its place: a black skull on blood red. No Lord's mark on it; any poacher on the Midarra can run that one up. The two-master leans into the wind and comes straight for you, and as she closes you can see her deck: crowded rail to rail, far more hands than a ship that size needs to sail her.</p><p>\"Poachers,\" says Tarrek, quite calmly, and starts herding the crew toward the hatch. \"Below. All of you. That's what we pay them for.\" Ozhra is already halfway down the ladder to the locked cabin. On the other ship, you see someone swinging a grapnel, then a shot whisks past your face.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>The fight</h4><p>Cold start into a hot opening. Redsail's crew is unflagged and poaching; the Goodmeasure flies no colours, so she is anyone's prize. The crew shelter below; the party fights alone, which is what they were hired for. Run the fight until the party is clearly winning, then cut to the broadside. Keep Redsail alive for it.</p>\n<h4>Encounter · Redsail's crew · 190 XP, near extreme (5 PCs at level 11)</h4>\n<p>Meant to be and feel very dangerous: the party never finishes this fight, Ninehulls does. One captain, two strong ones, and six troops as the mooks.</p>\n<p><b>Redsail</b> (Privateer Captain, level 11, 40 XP) · <b>the mate</b> (Intimidating Beserker, level 10, 30 XP) · <b>the knife</b> (Brutal Sharper, level 10, 30 XP) · <b>the boarders</b> (3 × Naval Crew troop, level 8, 45 XP) · <b>the gun crews</b> (3 × Black Powder Crew troop, level 8, 45 XP).</p>\n<h4>Redsail</h4>\n<p><em>Reskin: Privateer Captain (Lost Omens Character Guide) · Creature 11 · captain of an unflagged poacher · prays loudly to Shuun</em></p>\n<p><b>HP</b> 175 · <b>AC</b> 30 · <b>Perception</b> +21 · <b>Fort</b> +19 · <b>Ref</b> +20 · <b>Will</b> +23 · <b>Speed</b> 25 ft · Acrobatics +20, Deception +21, Religion +23, Thievery +22.</p>\n<p><b>Rapier</b> +21, 2d6+5 piercing (deadly d8, disarm) · <b>Crossbow</b> +21, 1d8+5 piercing (reload 1).</p>\n<p><b>Divine prepared spells</b> DC 30, attack +22: <i>blade barrier</i>, <i>repulsion</i> (6th) · <i>breath of life</i>, <i>control water</i> (5th) · <i>downpour</i>, <i>freedom of movement</i> (4th) · <i>blindness</i> (3rd) · <i>dispel magic</i>, <i>faerie fire</i>, <i>silence</i> and more (2nd) · <i>bane</i>, <i>gust of wind</i>, <i>harm</i>, <i>shield</i>, <i>tidal surge</i> (1st). <b>Reach Spell</b> (1 action). <b>Sink or Swim</b> (1 action, once per day): for 1 minute, enemies within 60 ft treat the water as turbulent (Athletics DC 20 to Swim) and a failed Swim becomes a critical failure.</p>\n<h4>Redsail's mate · Togafiti</h4>\n<p><em>Togafiti out of Rika Tikur · Reskin: Intimidating Beserker lvl 10 (Jam and Jax, NPC Index: Warriors) · Creature 10 · a boarding-axe brute</em></p>\n<p><b>HP</b> 223 · <b>AC</b> 27 · <b>Perception</b> +22 · <b>Fort</b> +22 · <b>Ref</b> +18 · <b>Will</b> +16 · Speed 25 ft.</p>\n<p><b>+1 striking fauchard</b> +23, 2d8+24 slashing (deadly d8, reach 15 ft, sweep, trip) · <b>Crossbow</b> +20, 2d8+10 piercing. <b>Instant Rage</b> on initiative; <b>Giant's Stature</b> (Large, reach +5 ft, clumsy 1); <b>No Escape</b> (reaction: keeps pace with a foe moving away); <b>Terrifying Howl</b> (2 actions: Demoralize every enemy within 30 ft).</p>\n<h4>The knife · Naama</h4>\n<p><em>Naama out of Solkai · Reskin: Brutal Sharper lvl 10 (Jam and Jax, NPC Index: Specialists) · Creature 10 · two daggers and no manners</em></p>\n<p><b>HP</b> 178 · <b>AC</b> 29 · <b>Perception</b> +22 · <b>Fort</b> +16 · <b>Ref</b> +22 · <b>Will</b> +19 · Speed 25 ft.</p>\n<p><b>+1 striking dagger</b> +21, 2d6+10 piercing (agile, finesse, versatile S; thrown 10 ft) · <b>Crossbow</b> +21, 2d6+9 piercing. <b>Twin Feint</b> (2 actions: a Strike with each dagger; the target is off-guard against the second) · <b>Sneak Attack</b> (precision damage per the sheet) · <b>Debilitating Strikes</b> (on a hit against an off-guard target: −10 ft Speed or enfeebled 1) · <b>Nimble Dodge</b> (reaction: +2 AC) · Deny Advantage, Blind-Fight.</p>\n<h4>The boarders (×3) · the gun crews (×3)</h4>\n<p><em>Naval Crew and Black Powder Crew (Lost Omens High Seas) · Creature 8 troops · Gargantuan, 4 segments</em></p>\n<p><b>HP</b> 135 each · <b>AC</b> 26 · <b>Perception</b> +16 · <b>Fort</b> +15 · <b>Ref</b> +18 · <b>Will</b> +14 · Speed 25 ft · Athletics +18 · <b>Weakness</b> area 10, splash 10 · Troop Defenses, Troop Movement, Sea Legs.</p>\n<p><b>Coordinated Cutlasses</b> (1 to 3 actions, once per round): every enemy in a 5-ft emanation, basic Reflex DC 23; 1d6+2 / 3d6+6 / 4d6+8 slashing. <b>Repel Boarders!</b> (1 action): one Athletics check to Shove every adjacent enemy in a chosen direction. <b>Rock the Boat</b> (2 actions, on a ship): the troop Strides, then everyone else aboard makes Reflex DC 26 or falls prone.</p>\n<p>The boarders add <b>Crossbow Salvo</b> (3 actions: 10-ft burst within 60 ft, 5d6 piercing, basic Reflex DC 23). The gun crew add <b>Pistol Salvo</b> (2 actions, once per 10 minutes: 10-ft burst within 40 ft, 7d4 piercing, basic Reflex DC 23; a critical failure takes 10 more after doubling). Flintlocks of the Saegate pattern, bought through Gesalkai.</p>\n<h4>Who's here · Redsail's ship</h4>\n<p>Redsail's two-master carries far more crew than the troops on the map: the rest work the sails and the guns and wait their turn at the rail. Ninehulls' broadside kills many of them. The survivors are the ones who hold the Last Hands over Redsail and sign under the black flag, and the ones the party can question afterwards.</p>\n<ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Teofoga out of Hringseyja</b> · quartermaster: never draws, calls the Last Hands over Redsail</li><li><b>Togafiti out of Rika Tikur</b> · the mate (stat block above)</li><li><b>Naama out of Solkai</b> · the knife (stat block above)</li></ul>\n<h4>Running the fight</h4>\n<p><b>Round 1:</b> grapnels and a boarding plank at the port rail. The three gun crews stay on their own deck and open with Pistol Salvo across the gap, one after another; all three boarder troops and the mate come over the plank, and the mate howls first. The knife comes over the bow on a line and goes for whoever the boarders have knocked prone or flanked.</p>\n<p><b>Then:</b> the boarders Rock the Boat to put the party on the deck and use Repel Boarders! to shove them toward the rail; anyone who goes over is in the Midarra, and Redsail answers with Sink or Swim. Redsail stays on his own quarterdeck and casts: <i>blade barrier</i> across the rail, <i>bane</i>, <i>downpour</i>.</p>\n<p><b>The pressure:</b> six troops are more bodies than the Goodmeasure's deck can hold. Fill the port rail and the main deck with them, keep the gun crews firing from the other ship once their salvos are spent (they board after), and let the party see Redsail's ship still has more on it than they have.</p>\n<p><b>The cut:</b> after two or three rounds, or as soon as the party is clearly holding (a troop broken, a strong one down, or Redsail himself in danger), Ninehulls' broadside lands. If it goes badly for the party, it lands sooner. The troops' weakness to area damage is what makes cannon shred them; Redsail survives it, for Ninehulls.</p>\n<p><b>The bought name:</b> Redsail calls his own name like a battle-cry; his crew do not echo it. A Society check (DC 25, the Twin Cities' tellers' trade) or anyone who has heard Freeboard's taverns knows nobody tells of Redsail.</p>\n<h4>Still to build</h4><ul class=\"trait-list todo\"></ul>\n<!-- map: /gm-notes/short-notice/quest-the-unspent/maps/goodmeasure-deck -->\n<!-- /map -->"}, {"name": "2 · Ninehulls' Broadside", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Social · the Pirate Lord</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Ninehulls · Halfpenny · Redsail</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>Something cracks the sky open, so loud you feel it in your teeth. For a heartbeat the world is only ringing.</p><p>Then the thunder comes again, and again, and again: a rolling line of cracks, one on the heels of the next, and you feel every one of them in the wood under your feet. In the next breath the poachers' rail has stopped existing, along with some of its crew.</p><p>Out of the haze to starboard come two black-hulled ships, flying the same flag: black, with a red nine painted on it, a skull grinning out of the loop of the nine and bleeding down into red water.</p><p>Then a third comes out of the smoke behind them, and the other two look like her boats. She is three-masted and broad as a warehouse, black canvas stacked up into the sky, two decks of gunports open down her side with the smoke still pouring out of them. Her hull is a patchwork: planks of other ships worked into the black, a strip of green paint here, a run of gilt scrollwork there, half of a merchant's painted name upside down along her waterline. From her mainmast flies the nine, so big the wind can barely lift it. Her rails and her rigging are packed with crew, and they are cheering.</p><p>Before the smoke clears a figure the size of a wardrobe swings across on a line and lands on your deck like a dropped anchor; the planks groan, and the whole ship dips toward him. He straightens up, a head above anyone aboard, and looks the poachers over with real disappointment. \"Now what,\" he asks, \"are you doing in my waters?\"</p><p>Redsail answers for them. \"Redsail!\" he roars, and charges, rapier out. \"You've heard of Redsail!\"</p><p>The big man lets the point skid off the front of his coat. One hand closes on Redsail's throat and lifts him off the deck; the other brings the cutlass up under his ribs and out between his shoulders. Redsail kicks, a child struggling against a mountain. A gurgle, his clothes darken to the colour of his flag. Ninehulls holds him up until he stops, then lets him fall in a heap at his boots and wipes the blade on his sleeve. \"Red-What?\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>What happens</h4><p>Over in a breath: a nobody against a legend. The rest of the scene is the surrender, in three beats.</p><p><img alt=\"Ninehulls' flag: a red nine on black, a skull in its loop, bleeding into red water\" src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/ninehulls-flag.webp\"/><p class=\"todo\">Ninehulls' flag</p></p>\n<h3>Beat 2 · Weapons down</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>For a moment nobody on deck moves. Then a cutlass hits the planks, and another, and the poachers' weapons go down one after another until the deck rings with them. Somebody's crossbow goes off into the sail as it lands. Nobody laughs.</p><p>The big man looks at the pile, then at you, and his whole face changes: the eyes crinkle, and the smile comes out with every tooth in it.</p><p>\"My apologies,\" he says, and means it. \"Truly. You were having a nice quiet crossing, and this lot came and spoiled it, in my waters, which makes it my fault, near enough.\" He claps once. \"Ninehulls. You'll have heard.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Beat 3 · Redsail's ship goes down</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>Across the water the two-master is dying. Her mainmast has gone over the side in a tangle of canvas, there is a hole in her flank you could drive a cart through, and the lake pours in at it. She leans toward you, and her people come over your rail any way they can: down the grapnel lines, across the boarding planks, a few in the water, swimming hard, two of them dragging a sea-chest between them.</p><p>Behind the last of them she rolls onto her side, shows her keel once, green with weed, and goes under with a long belch of air. The red flag goes last.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Beat 4 · Your turn</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>More of his people are coming over now, swinging down from the black ships on lines, dozens of them, landing light and spreading along your rails with pistols in their belts and no hurry at all. On the great ship's rail a row of long guns follows you as you move.</p><p>Ninehulls turns back to you, still smiling. \"Now. Be dears and put those down too, would you? Nobody's in any trouble. I'd just hate for anyone to get excited.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Running it</h4><p>His tone is the whole threat. He never raises his voice, and he does not need to: three ships and a full crew answer for him. If the players fight anyway, his crews board from all three ships at once and the scene ends badly for everyone; let them see that before they decide.</p><p>The weapons go into Halfpenny's keeping, counted, tagged and written down. They come back at the landing in Freeboard, every one, with a receipt.</p>"}, {"name": "3 · The Last Hands, at Sea", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Ritual · the players see it early</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Ninehulls · Teofoga out of Hringseyja · Halfpenny · Master Ozhra</p>\n<h3>Beat 1 · The vote</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>Redsail's crew stand over their captain's body with their hands at their sides. Nobody tells them what to do. One by one the hands go up.</p><p>\"Deposition,\" says the oldest of them, and then, louder, to the man with the black flag: \"We'll sail under you, if you'll have us.\" Ninehulls claps once. \"Course I will. Somebody get them a drink.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>What happens</h4><p>A killed captain gets the Last Hands: deposition frees the killer to stand for the seat, murder sees them marooned. Here it is quick and clear, so the players know the ritual when it comes back at the end. Teofoga, Redsail's quartermaster, calls the vote.</p>\n<h3>Beat 2 · The master of the ship</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>Two of Ninehulls' crew come up the ladder from below with Master Ozhra between them, a hand on each arm, his feet hunting for the rungs. Behind him the rest of the Goodmeasure's people are herded up into the light: Tarrek with his head down under the hatch, Shab with the ledger clutched to her chest, Hangas still holding his cleaver until someone gently takes it off him. Patala is talked down out of the nest last.</p><p>Ninehulls looks Ozhra over the way he looked at you, kindly, and bends a long way down to shake his hand. \"Master of the ship? A pleasure. A real pleasure. She's a lovely thing, isn't she? Kept well. You can always tell.\"</p><p>\"Now. I won't set you adrift in the jolly boat. I'm not an animal. I'll carry you to Freeboard, every one of you, fed and dry.\" The smile stays, and his voice drops to a rumble you feel through the deck. \"But this ship is mine. A deck in Freeboard needs a hull, and this one fits.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Running it</h4><p>Ozhra's hand goes to the key at his throat and stays there. He agrees, because there is nothing else to do; so, very likely, do the party. Shab looks at the locked cabin door once and then very hard at the deck. The locked cabin is Ninehulls' business now.</p>\n<h3>Beat 3 · All hands</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>Ninehulls straightens up and fills his chest, and when he shouts, the black ships hear it. \"Halfpenny! She's yours to Freeboard. Take twenty of ours. Redsail's lot, half aboard her and half with me; mix them up, I want them making friends. Get that rag off her mast. Let's go home!\"</p><p>The deck comes apart and puts itself back together around you. Strangers run up the shrouds, a line of hands passes Redsail's sea-chest over the rail, and a tall elf with ink-black fingertips and a brass half-penny at her throat steps aboard with a wax tablet, writing before her boots are dry. The trader's pennant comes down, and the red nine goes up in its place. Before the smoke has quite cleared, the Goodmeasure is under sail again, the black ships around her like an escort.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>The way home: time to talk</h4><p>A day and a night at sea, among the people who just tried to kill them, with Halfpenny captaining. Let the players wander and ask. The Goodmeasure's own crew are kept below by day and let up at dusk.</p><p><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Teofoga</b>: how Redsail bought his name, and from which teller; what Redsail meant to do with Ozhra's cargo. Easy company; he likes a careful listener.</li><li><b>Togafiti and Naama</b>, if they lived: sore losers, then not. Naama asks the party who they were before the Guild.</li><li><b>Halfpenny</b>: what the party are worth in shares, and why the Goodmeasure is worth more as a deck than as a ship. Asked about Ninehulls, she answers with the legend, word for word, and nothing else.</li><li><b>Ninehulls' crew</b>: the legend, many times, every telling a little bigger. Nine ships in one night. The wound that should have killed him. The man who did, who is dead now.</li><li><b>Ankhes Khata</b>: sneaks up at night to ask the pirates for stories, and the party for theirs.</li><li><b>Ozhra</b>: sits on a coil of rope at the stern and watches the sea, the key in his fist.</li></ul></p>"}, {"name": "4 · Freeboard", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Exploration · the stack</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Ninehulls · Pell out of the Spar · Odile Brasshand</p>\n<h3>Beat 1 · The stack</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>On the second morning the lookout calls, and you go up to see what Master Ozhra will not look at.</p><p>At first it looks like an island with a storm sitting on it. Then it comes closer, and the storm is masts: hundreds of them, standing out at every angle from a mountain of ships. Hulls stacked on hulls, black and brown and every colour paint has ever been, piled so high the top of it catches the sun while the water around its foot is still in shadow. Gangways and rope-bridges run between them like cobwebs. Smoke climbs from a dozen chimneys that used to be portholes.</p><p>Around its foot sails a ring of ships under canvas, keeping pace with the mountain, and it is only when you see them that you understand the mountain is moving. The noise reaches you before the smell does: bells, hammers, a hundred voices shouting about prices, somebody singing badly. Then the smell: tar, lamp oil, wet wood and, somewhere in all of it, fresh bread.</p><p>On the very top stand five ships stood on end like spires, each one flying its own flag, and one of them is a red nine on black. A sixth flies a flag faded almost to nothing.</p><p>Heads come up out of the water as you close with the ring, sleek and dark, and watch you pass: Merfolk, keeping pace with the hull without seeming to swim.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Beat 2 · The landing</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>The Goodmeasure comes in under the stack's shadow and makes fast at a landing of old hulls lashed flat, where the boats tie up three deep. Halfpenny hands your weapons back one by one, with a receipt.</p><p>You are hardly off the gangway when the chains come down. Two great booms built from old masts swing out from the stack above you, the chains bite under the Goodmeasure's hull, and with a shout and a groan of winches she lifts out of the water. Lake water pours off her keel in sheets. She turns slowly in the air as she rises, past the first deck, the second, the third, toward a gap in the mountain that is exactly her size.</p><p>Ninehulls stands beside you watching her go, his hands on his hips, like a man showing off his house. \"She'll make a lovely deck,\" he says.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>What happens</h4><p>Ozhra, his crew and the party go free on the landing. Ozhra goes looking for a ship home without a word to anyone; his crew go after him, Ankhes last and looking back. The party are on their own, with their weapons and their purses, in the city that asks no questions.</p>\n<h3>Beat 3 · Pell</h3>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>A small woman cuts through the crowd on the landing like she owns it, and it parts for her. A halfling, freckled, grey at the temples, in a long coat sewn all over with coins that chime as she walks.</p><p>\"You're the Goodmeasure's guards.\" It is not a question. \"Off Ninehulls' prize. Don't look like that, the whole Spar had it before your boots were dry.\" She looks you over, one at a time, like a merchant pricing a cargo. \"Pell, out of the Spar. I tell for a living. Names, please, and out of where. And then a tale.\"</p><p>\"Anyone can tell a capture. I want the words. What did he say when he came over the rail? Exactly. And what did you do?\" She smiles. \"First drink's mine, at the Fairturn. Second's yours, if the room asks for it.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Running it</h4><p>Pell trades: a drink and directions for the tale. Whatever they tell her, she tells tonight at the <b>Fairturn</b>, bigger and better, and the party are in it by name. If the players keep it to themselves, Ninehulls tells it anyway, in his own version where he saved them from the poachers, and by the next watch half the Spar has heard.</p><p><b>Their tale spreads from here on, wherever they go.</b> Strangers know them by the capture. That is how Merrin finds them.</p>\n<h3>Beat 4 · The Lower Spar</h3>\n<p class=\"todo\">Where they go between landing and the Mooring. Each place has a walk-in read-aloud and what it offers.</p>"}, {"name": "Freeboard · The Fairturn", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>foot of the Lower Spar · tavern · kept by Rosalba out of the Fairturn</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>The door is a ship's hatch turned on its side, and the noise comes out of it like heat. Inside, the room is the whole hold of a ship, three floors of it, open to the beams, with ladders and galleries running up the walls and every floor packed. Lanterns everywhere. On the ground floor a teller stands on a table with a tankard in each hand, halfway through somebody's death, and the room is shouting along with the good parts.</p><p>Behind the bar, a broad dwarf woman with a grey braid pinned up with a fork chalks a new line onto a slate as big as a door: whatever came in last, over whatever came in before.</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Drinks</b> are whatever the last prize carried; ask Rosalba what is on and she reads the slate aloud, ship by ship.</li><li><b>Rooms</b> in the hulls above: comfortable lodging at the usual price, with a porthole each.</li><li><b>Tellers</b> on every floor: the ground floor tells anything, the top floor tells the season's best. Pell tells here, and tells the party's capture the night they land.</li><li><b>Rumours</b>: Rosalba hears everything said on three floors. Freeboard canon on the Lords, the Last Hands and the Mooring is all common talk here.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Freeboard · The Lost Property", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>halfway along the Spar · prize goods · kept by Nohea out of the Lost Property</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>A whole hull, gutted and shelved from keel to deck, and every shelf crammed: rope, lanterns, boots, cookpots, sea-chests, a figurehead with no nose. Over each shelf hangs a painted board with a ship's name on it, some of them scratched out and repainted. It smells of tar and other people's pockets.</p><p>A small goblin with a jeweller's loupe in one eye pops up from behind a stack of crates. \"Welcome, welcome. What are you after, and off which ship?\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Common and uncommon gear</b> up to level 11 at <b>three quarters of list price</b>, sold as found. No returns, no questions, no history.</li><li>Goods carry their old owners' initials; Nohea scrapes them off for a copper.</li><li>Ask for a thing by its ship and he finds it at once; ask by kind and he sighs.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Freeboard · The Great Cabin", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>on the Spar, hoisted · magic items · kept by Ottavia out of Namur</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>You climb a ladder to a door in the side of a ship's stern, hung out over the Spar, and step into a captain's cabin cut whole out of its ship. The tall leaded stern windows are still in it, with the lanterns of the stack outside them instead of the sea. Everything is laid out where it was found: a wand on the captain's desk beside a half-written letter, a sword still in its rack, rings in an open sea-chest, a coat on the back of the chair.</p><p>A tall elf in a salt-stained blue coat looks up from her spectacles, and her eyes go to your hands first. \"Welcome. Touch nothing until I've told you what it did.\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Magic items</b>, permanent and consumable, up to <b>level 12</b>, at list price, each sold with its tale.</li><li>A piece with a famous tale (it killed a captain, it sank a ship) costs <b>up to half again</b>. A buyer who wants a piece <b>clean</b>, its tale left behind, pays <b>a tenth extra</b>.</li><li>Ottavia buys magic too, at half price, and pays more for a good story. The party's capture is a story.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Freeboard · The Wash", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>two decks under the Spar · fighting ring · kept by Holdfast</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>Down two ladders and the air turns wet and cold. The hold below has been opened to the lake on purpose: black water fills it to within a man's height of the gallery, and on the water floats a ring of old hatch-covers, lashed loosely together, rocking. A crowd packs the gallery all the way round, shouting down. Two fighters are out on the covers, and one of them is losing his footing.</p><p>In the water by the ladder, a Merfolk woman with a brass chain over her shoulders folds her arms on a floating plank and grins up at you. \"New faces. Fighting or betting?\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Bouts</b> run on the floating covers. At the start of each turn a fighter makes <b>Acrobatics DC 25 to Balance</b> or is off-guard until their next turn. <b>In the water, you lose.</b> A Shove that moves a fighter off the covers ends the bout. Still standing at the bell (three rounds): it goes to the hands of the crowd.</li><li><b>House fighters</b>: a level 9 to 11 brawler from the bestiary, reskinned. Purse <b>100 gp</b> a win; Holdfast takes bets at even money, two to one against a newcomer.</li><li>The Merfolk fish the loser out for <b>1 gp</b>. A fighter who throws a bout meets Holdfast under the water.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Freeboard · The Stillroom", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>below the waterline, by the engines · alchemist · kept by Kahu out of the Low Hatch</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>Down past the dry holds, where the planks sweat and you can hear the lake on the other side of them, a door stands open on warm green light. The Stillroom is hot from the engines next door and smells of weed and vinegar. Glassware bubbles on every bench. A hatch in the floor stands open on dark water, a bucket of eels beside it, and an axe hangs on the wall by the door.</p><p>A small mottled tripkee in a stained apron looks round at you through smoked goggles. \"Shut the door. Not that one. That one's for the fire.\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Alchemical consumables</b> up to <b>level 11</b> at list price: elixirs, bombs, poisons, tools.</li><li>Kahu <b>buys monster parts</b> and alchemical reagents, and pays well for anything from a creature she has never seen.</li><li>Her own blend: <b>deck-legs</b>, a draught for seasickness that works, mostly (no mechanical effect beyond comfort; she swears by it).</li></ul>"}, {"name": "5 · The Mooring", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Set-piece · the sky comes home</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Kesti Downdraft · Odile Brasshand</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>It starts as a shout somewhere high up, and it comes down the stack deck by deck, gangway by gangway, until the whole city is shouting it: <i>the sky! The sky's coming home!</i> Doors bang open. The promenades empty upward. Everyone climbs: up ladders that used to be masts, up rope-lifts packed to the rails, up the outsides of hulls hand over hand. Children are already on the spires, and the spire crews are not bothering to chase them off.</p><p>You come out onto a high deck into wind and daylight, and see them.</p><p>Out in the west, low over the water, four islands are coming home. Dark rock underneath, bearded with roots that trail in the wind, and along the top of each the edge of a city glinting in the sun. Under every one hangs a cluster of airships on long lines drawn tight as bowstrings, straining, like gulls carrying something too heavy for them and too precious to drop.</p><p>They come on slowly, and they grow, and keep growing. The first shadow reaches the ring of ships at the stack's foot and climbs the mountain toward you, and the air goes cold. Then they are overhead, so close you can see faces at the edges looking down at you, and a sound comes with them: a low, many-voiced hum, the wind singing through a whole city of open windows.</p><p>They stop. They hang there over Freeboard, and as they settle they shed their clouds: a cold, fine rain falls out of a clear sky onto every upturned face on the stack, and the whole city cheers it.</p><p>Then the lines come down. Baskets drop from the islets on ropes, gangways swing out and bang down onto the highest decks, and people come pouring across in both directions. By midnight the two cities are one market, fruit from the sky and fish from the pens and prize goods from both, and everyone shouting about the price of everything.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>What happens</h4><p>Skysail moors over Freeboard; the two Lords and the Pirate Lords sit together, and the party can see Kesti Downdraft and Odile Brasshand before they need either of them. The baskets carry anyone up who pays the basket-crew.</p>\n<h3>Places on Skysail</h3>\n<p class=\"todo\">Up by basket once the cities are moored.</p>"}, {"name": "Skysail · The Edge", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>along the drop on the Main · tables and kitchen · kept by Graça out of the Main</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>The square simply stops. Along the end of it runs a line of tables under striped awnings, and past the tables there is nothing: open air, and far below, the sea of cloud. Hammocks hang out over the drop from posts sunk in the rock, and people are asleep in them. Everyone at the tables sits with their back to the edge.</p><p>A tall strix woman with flour on her wingtips sets a plate of sky-pears in front of you before you have sat down. \"Back to the drop, the first week. Everyone does.\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Food and drink</b>: sky fruit, cold tea, fish from the Freeboard pens on Mooring days. Cheap and very good.</li><li><b>Kesti Downdraft's table</b> is the one at the end. It stays empty while she is away, and she can be found there on a long afternoon.</li><li>Skysail's talk: which winds are coming, which crews are out, and the Jigger's cold.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Skysail · The Ropewalk", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>under the Jigger, on its own lines · rope and rigging · kept by Jowan out of the Jigger</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>You climb down through a hatch in the rock and come out under the Jigger, into the wind. The Ropewalk is a gallery of planks and netting hung on lines beneath the islet, longer than any room you have ever stood in, open to the air on both sides. Rope runs its whole length on pegs, and people walk backward along it, twisting. The cold here bites.</p><p>At the far end, so close you could read her name, hangs a dark airship with black sails, on lines of her own. Nobody at the Ropewalk looks at her for long.</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Rope, rigging and airship gear</b> at list price, made to measure.</li><li>The keepers mend the Unspent's lines here; <b>Merrin and her people</b> can be found at the far end.</li><li>Jowan knows every line under the Jigger and how much weight each one carries. He does not like the idea of anyone boarding her.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "Skysail · The Tuning House", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>on the Fore · wind-tuner · kept by Ilta out of the Fore</em></p><blockquote><p><strong>Going in</strong></p><p>The house sings before you reach it: a low chord in the wind, three notes, then four. Inside, the walls are almost all window, every opening a different shape, and bells, chimes and pipes hang in all of them. Stone samples line the shelves, each tapped and labelled. It is the quietest loud room you have ever been in.</p><p>A small blue-black tengu with a dozen whistles round their neck tilts their head at you. \"You speak in a flat B. Most of Freeboard does. Come in.\"</p></blockquote><h4>What's here</h4><ul class=\"trait-list\"><li><b>Wind-bells, chimes and whistles</b>; skiff pilots' signal whistles; tuning for a house or a ship's rigging.</li><li>Ilta hears everything the wind carries on the Fore. Asked about the Jigger, they say its note has been wrong for as long as they have been alive.</li></ul>"}, {"name": "6 · The Hire", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Social · the keepers' captain</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cast: </strong>Merrin out of the Jigger</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Read Aloud</strong></p><p>She finds you, which tells you something: a young woman in a coat two sizes too grand for her, with the flat, hungry look of someone who has just been voted into a job.</p><p>\"Merrin, out of the Jigger.\" She sits down without being asked. \"They're telling you on both cities. Guild, off Ninehulls' prize, and the poachers who tried you are dead or signed on. They're also saying you're a long way from dry land, with no ship of your own and nobody here who owes you a passage.\"</p><p>\"I have two ships that fly.\" She lets that sit. \"And there's a third, under the Jigger, that nobody has boarded in a hundred and forty years. She's ours by right. Open her for me, and my keepers will set you down anywhere on the coast you like.\"</p></blockquote>\n<h4>What happens</h4><p>The keepers are the grandchildren of the crews of Goldwake's other two airships. They are broke and voted Merrin in on the promise to open the Unspent; Nirfel has been whispering to them. None of them will board her. Her offer: passage to any coast on a keepers' airship, and a share of the sale of what is inside.</p><p>Up by basket to the Unspent, hanging under the Jigger.</p>\n<h4>Still to build</h4><ul class=\"trait-list todo\"><li>Merrin's offer as numbers (an appraisal fee, a share on sale).</li></ul>\n<h3>End of Chapter 1 · Struck Colours</h3>"}]}, {"name": "The Unspent · Cast", "pages": [{"name": "Ninehulls", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/ninehulls.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Ninehulls' Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>Pirate Lord of the sea · the man who cannot die · Full</strong></p>\n<p><em>Took nine ships in one night. A wide smile, real manners, and a fleet behind him. Apologises to the party for the poachers and takes their ship anyway.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Human · about 50</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>A Pirate Lord of the sea</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Built with the final fight: a level below the boss budget, so The Man Who Cannot Die can carry his second life</p><p><strong>Size: </strong>Two metres thirty, built like a wardrobe: a Large token. He grows a hair with every telling, a running joke on the Midarra that is true.</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Square in every direction: shoulders a doorframe wide, hands that make a tankard look like a thimble, deep sun-brown skin. Scalp shaved clean; a thick black beard in heavy curled plaits bound with brass rings. A pale, puckered scar runs across his throat and down his chest, from the wound that should have killed him and started the legend; he leaves his shirt open to show it. Eyes that crinkle; a wide smile with every tooth still in it.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A long black captain's coat, so much cloth that the tellers say it was cut from the mainsail of the first of the nine, lined in the red of his flag and patched wherever blades have found him, a red sash wound at the waist. No hat: nothing fits. Bare forearms, heavy boots, and a cutlass forged to his own scale, an ordinary sword in his hand and a two-hander in anyone else's.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Warm and booming, never in a hurry, courteous to a fault. Apologises sincerely and takes your ship anyway. Laughs at himself before anyone else can.</p><p><strong>Sample lines: </strong>\"Now what are you doing in my waters?\" · \"I won't set you adrift in the jolly boat. I'm not an animal. But the ship's mine.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Claps once when he has decided something. Ducks every beam in Freeboard with the ease of a man who has hit every one of them once.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly and amused toward the party, until the tellers start telling them bigger than him</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>To be told. Every raid, every apology and every round he pays for is a story.</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>His fleet and crews · Halfpenny, his quartermaster</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive; dies to the party at the end, and walks into their tavern three nights later</p><section class=\"secret\"><p><strong>⚿ GM Secret · What he is</strong></p><p>The man died in an ambush in Freeboard. The Midarra believed he could not die, and the belief made a being shaped as him, which knows only the story and has no given name. It struck down the man the taverns blamed, who was the wrong man. It lives on being told; a forgotten Lord stops being. Canon: <i>lore/geography/askamira/twin-cities.md</i>, ⚿ Ninehulls.</p></section>"}, {"name": "Halfpenny", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/halfpenny.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Ninehulls' Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>Ninehulls' quartermaster · a told name · Full</strong></p>\n<p><em>A ledger that walks. Counts everything, including you, and tells you the total.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 11 and Non-Combat Level 11 (the books, the shares).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Mercantile Lore</th><th>Society</th><th>Intimidation</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+26</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+24</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+24</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Mercantile Lore DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>34</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>34</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>36</strong><br/>slip a bad figure past her</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Elf · about 180</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Quartermaster of Ninehulls' flagship; captain of the Goodmeasure for the run to Freeboard</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 11 · Non-Combat Level 11 (the books, the shares) · full stat block with the Ninehulls fight</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Tall and spare, with silver-grey hair cropped short against the wind, a long patient face and ink worked so deep into her fingertips it will never wash out. A worn brass half-penny hangs on a cord at her throat: the coin the tellers say she split a prize down to.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A long sea-coat with more pockets than seams, a tally-stick in every one; sleeves rolled to the elbow; a wax tablet and stylus at her hip where another officer would wear a pistol. Good boots, badly kept.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>A quartermaster's dry arithmetic: numbers as punctuation, never a wasted word, never raised.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"You're worth eleven shares on that ship and three on this one. Don't make me count you twice.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Taps the half-penny when she is deciding; writes before she answers; looks at hands, not faces, during a vote.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Friendly to anyone who takes a fair share and no more</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Every share even, every hand paid, the books true. Ninehulls' crew stay his because she makes it worth it.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>Earned her name splitting a prize before the hands down to the half-penny. Has sailed with Ninehulls since before the legend. Calls the Last Hands over him at the end.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Shuun before a crossing; Jianna at the share-out</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>Ninehulls (loyal to the man, and to whatever came back as him) · respects Odile Brasshand, a quartermaster who rose</p><p><strong>Fear: </strong>An uneven share, and a crew that notices it</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive</p><section class=\"secret\"><p><strong>⚿ Secret</strong></p><p>She has noticed that the Ninehulls who came back remembers only what the tellers tell. She has told no one.</p></section>"}, {"name": "Redsail", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/redsail.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Redsail's Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>Poacher captain · a bought name · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>A big voice in a borrowed coat.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Straight off his stat block (Privateer Captain, Creature 11).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Religion</th><th>Thievery</th><th>Deception</th><th>Acrobatics</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Deception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>33</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>see through the boasting</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Human · 38</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Captain of an unflagged poacher two-master</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 11 (Privateer Captain reskin; stat block in Struck Colours)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Broad and sunburned, with a beard dyed the red of his sail, gold rings on every finger and a red sash wound twice round his middle. Good teeth he shows a lot.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Loud; announces himself; talks about himself in the third person when excited.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Redsail! You've heard of Redsail!\"</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Hostile</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>A told name that someone asks for twice.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>Paid a teller for his name before he had the deed. Nobody asked for the second telling. Prays to Shuun loudly and often.</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Dies at the opening, to Ninehulls.</p>"}, {"name": "Teofoga out of Hringseyja", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/teofoga.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Redsail's Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>Quartermaster · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 6 , and Non-Combat Level 9 for the shares.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Mercantile Lore</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>31</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>28</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>he/him · Lizardfolk · about 70 · Level 6, Non-Combat Level 9 (the shares)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Old olive scales gone grey at the jaw, one eye milky, a slow blink; never seen to hurry.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Deposition. Write it down, someone.\"</p><p><strong>Knows: </strong>How Redsail bought his name, and from which teller; what Redsail meant to do with the Goodmeasure's cargo.</p>"}, {"name": "Togafiti out of Rika Tikur", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/togafiti.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Redsail's Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>The mate · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<p><em>A brute who ends things now, head-on.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Straight off his stat block (Intimidating Berserker, Creature 10).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Athletics</th><th>Intimidation</th><th>Survival</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Fortitude DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>26</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>shove · grapple</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>he/him · Orc · about 30 · Level 10 (stat block above)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Huge, tusks ringed in iron, a red headscarf, scars he names; grows bigger in a rage.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Finish it.\"</p>"}, {"name": "Naama out of Solkai", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/naama.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Redsail's Crew</em></p>\n<p><strong>The knife · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<p><em>Very still, until she is not.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Straight off her stat block (Brutal Sharper, Creature 10).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Stealth</th><th>Deception</th><th>Acrobatics</th><th>Thievery</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Reflex DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>29</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>trip · disarm</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>she/her · Fetchling · about 28 · Level 10 (stat block above)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Shadow-grey skin, silver eyes, two daggers worn crosswise at the small of her back; very still until she is not.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Who you were is your business. Who you are is mine now.\"</p>"}, {"name": "Master Ozhra", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/ozhra.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Master of the Goodmeasure · Kholo · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>A careful man pretending very hard to be calm.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 2 for the body and Non-Combat Level 10 as a merchant.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Mercantile Lore</th><th>Deception</th><th>Diplomacy</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+8</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+5</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Deception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>32</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>29</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>read his question about the Lord's ship</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Kholo · about 55</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Master and owner of the stillship Goodmeasure; an important merchant of the Solkai crossing</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 2 · Non-Combat Level 10 (merchant)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Grizzled, with a spotted coat gone grey at the muzzle and one ear notched long ago. Ledger ink on the fingers of both hands. Watches the horizon more than his crew.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A good wool coat cut for a merchant, Solkai brass buttons polished; a key on a chain round his neck that he touches when he thinks no one sees.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Soft, precise; answers a question with a question.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"You'd know a Lord's ship, would you? At a distance, I mean.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Paces bow to wheel and back; touches the key; thanks people too warmly.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly (he hired them)</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Get the cargo to Solkai, and keep his own.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>Of a Kholo ferry-clan of the Solkai crossing; thirty crossings behind him. Trusts steel over pennants on this run.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Sarrum at home; Shuun before a crossing</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>His niece <b>Shab</b>, the purser · his crew (Struck Colours)</p><p><strong>Fear: </strong>A Lord's ship that knows what's in the locked cabin</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive; loses the Goodmeasure to Ninehulls and goes free in Freeboard</p><section class=\"secret\"><p><strong>⚿ Secret</strong></p><p>He bought no colours on purpose, and the locked cabin holds an eight-stripe Catjomin Sake and a case of temple-stamped dream-blends (Struck Colours, the locked cabin).</p></section>"}, {"name": "Tarrek", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/tarrek.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Bosun · Minotaur · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 4 , and Non-Combat Level 6 for sailing.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Sailing Lore</th><th>Athletics</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>24</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>24</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>he/him · Minotaur · about 45 · Level 4, Non-Combat Level 6 (sailing)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Huge and unhurried, horns capped in old brass, muzzle greying; a vine tattoo winds round one forearm from the terrace his family grows.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Grain's like grapes. You can't hurry either.\"</p>"}, {"name": "Shab", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/shab.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Purser · Kholo · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Non-Combat Level 4 (the books).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Mercantile Lore</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Diplomacy DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>24</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>21</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>21</strong><br/>press her about the cabin</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>she/her · Kholo · 26 · Non-Combat Level 4 (the books) · Ozhra's niece</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Spotted and sharp-eared, spectacles pushed up her muzzle, the ledger never out of her arms.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Uncle pays for what he trusts.\"</p>"}, {"name": "Hangas", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/hangas.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cook · Dragonet · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Non-Combat Level 6 (the galley).</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Cooking Lore</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>24</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>24</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>he/him · Dragonet · about 90 · Non-Combat Level 6 (the galley)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and dark-scaled like old copper, a curl of smoke from his nostrils when the stove is hot, a cleaver he uses for everything.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Eat. You're guards, not ghosts.\"</p>"}, {"name": "Ankhes Khata", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/ankhes-khata.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Deckhand · Duskwalker · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 1 .</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Athletics</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+7</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on them</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>17</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>17</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>they/them · Duskwalker · 19 · Level 1</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Pale-eyed and ash-pale, quick grin, bare feet black with tar, a knot of rope charms at the wrist.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Have you ever fought a dragon? Have you ever fought two?\"</p>"}, {"name": "Patala Latasi", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/patala-latasi.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Goodmeasure</em></p>\n<p><strong>Lookout · Goloma · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 3 ; the eyes are world-class.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+14</strong><br/>Extreme</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>19</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>24</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Who: </strong>she/her · Goloma · 33 · Level 3</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Tall and narrow, many eyes in a slow ring that never all close at once; lives in the crow's nest and comes down only to eat.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Sail!\"</p>"}, {"name": "Pell out of the Spar", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/pell.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>A teller of the Lower Spar · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>A market-woman who sells stories by the measure.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 2 for the body and Non-Combat Level 9 for the telling.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Performance</th><th>Society</th><th>Deception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+5</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+8</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Deception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>31</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>28</strong><br/>tell the true telling from the told</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Halfling · 40</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Teller: tells the Lords' deeds in the taverns for coin</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 2 · Non-Combat Level 9 (telling)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and quick, freckled, with a voice twice her size and a mobile face that does half the telling. Grey at the temples, laugh lines deep.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A teller's coat sewn with coins from every port on the Midarra, tips from rooms that asked for a second telling. Silver-buckled shoes off some merchant's feet, polished for the stage.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>A working storyteller's patter; talks about legends as stock to be kept, and about money plainly.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Anyone can buy a telling. Nobody can buy the second one.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Tries a phrase out under her breath before she uses it; counts the room before she starts.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; interested the moment the party becomes a story</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>The best story of the season, and the room asking for it twice.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>City-born on the Lower Spar. Has told Ninehulls a thousand times. Tells the party's capture before they have reached a tavern.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Cronus for freedom, Bikiargi for the night watch</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>Every tavern on the Spar · the Lords she tells</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive</p>"}, {"name": "Odile Brasshand", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/odile-brasshand.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>Lord of Freeboard · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>A quartermaster who never stopped counting, now counting a city.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 6 for the body and Non-Combat Level 12 for the seat.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Society</th><th>Diplomacy</th><th>Mercantile Lore</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+28</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+17</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+11</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Diplomacy DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>35</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>32</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>35</strong><br/>talk her off a number</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Human · about 50 · her family came out of Legea</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Lord of Freeboard (elected); a quartermaster who rose to the seat</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 6 · Non-Combat Level 12</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Square and weathered, close-cropped iron hair, a brass left hand where the flesh one used to be; the tellers tell how she lost it, and she does not.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Dry, numerate, unsentimental about Lords.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"You can't make peace with them. You can make arrangements with whichever one of them you're talking to.\"</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>One pennant that every Lord honours, and the Tenth to hold the stack together.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>Rose from quartermaster to Lord by the hands; lives on the Tenth and on colours.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Cronus, for freedom</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive · a cameo at the Mooring</p>"}, {"name": "Rosalba out of the Fairturn", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>Keeper of the Fairturn · Dwarf · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Runs the oldest room in Freeboard and remembers every tab ever left on it.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 3 for the body and Non-Combat Level 9 for the house.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Diplomacy</th><th>Society</th><th>Intimidation</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Low</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+6</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>28</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Dwarf · about 60</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Keeper of the Fairturn, Freeboard's first tavern; captain of its deck</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 3 · Non-Combat Level 9 (the house)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Broad and short, forearms like hams, a grey braid wound twice round her head and pinned with a fork. A burn scar across the back of one hand from the old stove.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A man's brocade waistcoat off some prize, buttoned wrong over a linen shirt, sleeves rolled; a leather apron; a ring of keys at her belt.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Loud enough to carry three floors without trying; calls everyone \"love\" and means nothing by it.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Board's on the slate, love. If it's rubbed out, it's gone.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Wipes the slate with her sleeve while she talks; knows which teller is on which floor without looking.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Friendly once they have paid for a round</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>A full house every watch, and a teller on the top floor the room asks for twice.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Cronus for freedom; Shuun when the city moves</p>"}, {"name": "Nohea out of the Lost Property", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>The Lost Property · Goblin · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Sells you your own lantern back, and knows which ship it came off.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 2 for the body and Non-Combat Level 8 for the trade.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Mercantile Lore</th><th>Thievery</th><th>Society</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+5</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+11</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Mercantile Lore DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>26</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>29</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>haggle him down</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Goblin · about 35</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Keeper of the Lost Property, the prize-goods hull on the Lower Spar</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 2 · Non-Combat Level 8 (trading)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and wiry, ears notched from old bargains, a jeweller's loupe screwed into one eye. Quick hands that are always holding something.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A captain's coat cut down to his size, the gold braid picked off and sold; three belts, each hung with tools; a scraping chisel on a cord.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Fast, cheerful, a patter of ship names; prices everything twice, once high.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Rope? Which ship? The Kittiwake's is cheaper, but she sank, so.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Scrapes initials off goods while he talks; never puts anything down on the counter, only into a hand.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly to anyone holding a purse</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Sell the whole hull before the next prize comes in.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Jianna at the till</p>"}, {"name": "Ottavia out of Namur", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>The Great Cabin · Elf · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Prices a wand by the man it killed.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 9 for the body and Non-Combat Level 11 for the appraisal; a real wizard if pushed.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Arcana</th><th>Society</th><th>Deception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+26</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+24</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Deception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>34</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>31</strong><br/>catch her padding a tale</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Elf · about 210</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Keeper of the Great Cabin; a ship's wizard once, until her ship was taken</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 9 · Non-Combat Level 11 (appraisal)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Tall and very straight, silver hair cut blunt at the jaw, a thin white scar round one wrist where a manacle sat for a year. Pale grey eyes that go to your hands first.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A ship's wizard's long blue coat, salt-stained and kept, its brass buttons each from a different navy; reading spectacles on a chain.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Quiet and exact, a teller's timing; tells each piece's tale before its price.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"This one killed a captain off Solkai. The price is the captain. The ring is extra.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Lays a piece down exactly where it was found; taps the glass of the stern window when she names a price.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>A piece with a tale good enough to keep.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Enki over a hard appraisal; Shuun, privately, for the ship she lost</p>"}, {"name": "Holdfast", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>The Wash's book · Merfolk · a told name · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Smiles up at you from the water and takes your bet.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 8 , combat and acuity alike; under water she is the strongest thing in the Wash.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Athletics</th><th>Games Lore</th><th>Intimidation</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+13</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th><th>Athletics DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>23</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>26</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td><td><strong>28</strong><br/>escape her hold</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Merfolk · about 45</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Keeps the book at the Wash; her pod fishes the losers out</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 8 · Non-Combat Level 8 (the book)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Broad-shouldered, grey-green and scarred, a long dark tail barred like a pike's, hair cropped short. Strong hands with webbing between the fingers, and a wide, delighted smile.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>Nothing but a heavy brass chain round her shoulders, hung with a tally of fighters' rings, and a waxed slate tied to her wrist.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Warm and amused, comes up bubbling from just below the surface; calls the fighters by what they are worth.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Two to one on the dry one. You're the wet one, love, if you go in.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Raps the underside of the planks to call a bout; holds a winner's hand up out of the water like a prize fish.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly to a good fighter and to a bad bettor</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>A clean book and a crowd that bets.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Shuun</p>"}, {"name": "Kahu out of the Low Hatch", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Freeboard</em></p>\n<p><strong>The Stillroom · Tripkee · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Never more than an arm's length from the axe on the wall.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 4 for the body and Non-Combat Level 10 for the alchemy.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Crafting</th><th>Medicine</th><th>Nature</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+14</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+11</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>26</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>29</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Tripkee · about 30</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Alchemist of the Stillroom, below the waterline by the engines</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 4 · Non-Combat Level 10 (alchemy)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and damp-skinned, mottled green and bronze, big gold eyes behind smoked goggles pushed up her forehead. Burn-pale spots on her fingers.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A rubber-cloth apron stiff with stains, sleeves tied back with string, a bandolier of corked phials across her chest.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Soft and croaking, very precise about measures; tells you what a thing does and what it does to you.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Drink half now. The other half if you live.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Sniffs everything before she sells it; buys from the Merfolk through her own hatch by the bucket, mid-sentence.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Friendly to anyone who brings her monster parts</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>One good batch of something nobody else on the Midarra can make.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Shuun, and the lake behind the plank</p>"}, {"name": "Kesti Downdraft", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/kesti-downdraft.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Skysail</em></p>\n<p><strong>Lord of Skysail and a Pirate Lord · Tengu · Full</strong></p>\n<p><em>Brisk and practical: hands you the useful thing first, then goes back to her work.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 14 , combat and acuity alike.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Sailing Lore (sky)</th><th>Acrobatics</th><th>Diplomacy</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+31</strong><br/>Extreme</td><td><strong>+28</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+28</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+22</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+25</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+28</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+28</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>38</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>38</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Tengu · about 60</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Lord of Skysail (elected) and a Pirate Lord of the sky</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 14 · Non-Combat Level 14</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Lean and wind-hard, slate-grey feathers shading pale at the throat, amber eyes that rate you in a glance. A white streak runs down one wing where the tellers say a downdraft nearly took her ship and did not.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>Flight leathers polished by years of rope, a fleece-lined coat for the Jigger's cold, a skiff-pilot's goggles pushed up into the crest feathers. No jewellery but a whistle on a cord.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Short sentences, the useful fact first; a laugh like a gust.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Down there they ask which watch. Up here we ask which wind. The Jigger's the cold one; you'll want a coat.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Lands from skiffs that are still moving; reads the sky before she reads a face.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Friendly once the party is carrying the heart up for her</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Keep all four islets in the air, and her city out of Freeboard's floors.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>Both an elected Lord and a Pirate Lord at once. Commands outright while the Jigger falls. Pays the party coin and passage afterwards.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya, like the sky crews</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>Skysail · the Pirate Lords · Old Hobb (lends him as a guide) · Odile Brasshand (sits with her at the Mooring)</p><p><strong>Fear: </strong>An islet falling, and being the Lord it fell under</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive</p>"}, {"name": "Old Hobb out of the Jigger", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/old-hobb.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Skysail</em></p>\n<p><strong>A tender of the old work · Tengu · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>An old man who knows every step of the dance and not one reason for it.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 1 for the body and Non-Combat Level 8 for the rites.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Crafting (old work)</th><th>Religion (rites)</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+7</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+4</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+19</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>29</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>29</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Tengu · about 80</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Tender of the Jigger's old work</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 1 · Non-Combat Level 8 (the rites)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Feathers gone ash-grey and thin, a crooked forefinger that points at everything, a slow rolling walk. His eyes are sharp.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A tender's leather apron hung with brass tools worn smooth, a scarf against the Jigger's cold.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Hums between sentences; short answers; never wrong about where to step.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Wind goes in somewhere up yonder too. Always has.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Touches each brass plate three times and hums four notes; the Wake step of the seating.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Keep the rites, and get home for supper.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>A tender all his life, like his mother. Cannot make the outside climb.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya; the rites themselves</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive</p>"}, {"name": "Graça out of the Main", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Skysail</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cook of the Edge · Strix · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Feeds you at the drop and laughs when you look down.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 2 for the body and Non-Combat Level 7 for the kitchen.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Cooking Lore</th><th>Diplomacy</th><th>Acrobatics</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+17</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+8</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+8</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+11</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>22</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>28</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Strix · about 40</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Cook and keeper of the Edge, the table-row along the drop on the Main</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 2 · Non-Combat Level 7 (the kitchen)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Tall and long-armed, dark brown wings folded high behind her shoulders, the tips dusted with flour. Close-cropped black hair, a broad easy face.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A loose sleeveless shirt slit at the back for the wings, a striped apron, bare forearms marked with old oven burns.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Bright and teasing; feeds people before she asks their names.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Sit with your back to it. Everyone does, the first week.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Steps off the edge to fetch a dropped spoon and comes back up with it.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Every table full by the long afternoon.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya</p>"}, {"name": "Jowan out of the Jigger", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Skysail</em></p>\n<p><strong>Master of the Ropewalk · Ratfolk · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Knows every line under the Jigger by its weight.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 5 for the body and Non-Combat Level 8 for the rope.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Crafting</th><th>Sailing Lore (sky)</th><th>Athletics</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+13</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+13</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+16</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on him</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>23</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>26</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>he/him</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Ratfolk · about 55</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Master of the Ropewalk; lays rope for the sky crews, and for the keepers at cost</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 5 · Non-Combat Level 8 (rope)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Grey-muzzled and rope-thin, paws ridged with old callus, a tail with a kink in it from a line that ran. One ear pierced with a brass thimble.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A tarred canvas smock, fleece-lined against the Jigger's cold, a marlinspike through a loop at his hip.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Few words, all of them about rope; distrusts anything that is not tied.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"Every line under her's mine. She hasn't dropped yet.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Walks the gallery hand over hand along the rope, never the rail; looks at the Unspent and away.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Unfriendly to anyone who means to board her</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>No line parts on his watch.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya</p>"}, {"name": "Ilta out of the Fore", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Skysail</em></p>\n<p><strong>The Tuning House · Tengu · Semi</strong></p>\n<p><em>Hears your house singing out of key from across the islet.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 3 for the body and Non-Combat Level 9 for the tuning; the ears are world-class.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Crafting</th><th>Performance</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+20</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>Extreme</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+6</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+9</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+21</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+23</strong><br/>Extreme</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on them</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>31</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress</td><td><strong>33</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>they/them</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Tengu · about 50</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Wind-tuner of the Tuning House on the Fore</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 3 · Non-Combat Level 9 (tuning)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and sleek, blue-black feathers with a pale bar across each wing, a beak nicked at the tip. Head always tilted, listening.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A loose grey robe tied at the waist with cord, a dozen whistles on strings round the neck, a little hammer for tapping stone.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Hums between words to find the note; describes people by the key they speak in.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"You speak in a flat B. It's not your fault. Most of Freeboard does.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Tilts their head at every window; plays a whistle instead of saying yes.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Indifferent; Friendly to anyone with a good ear</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>A whole islet in one chord.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya, the wind itself</p>"}, {"name": "Merrin out of the Jigger", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/merrin.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>The Unspent's Keepers</em></p>\n<p><strong>Captain of the Unspent's keepers · Full</strong></p>\n<p><em>Someone who just got the job she wanted, and the debt that came with it.</em></p>\n<h4>At the Table · Numbers</h4><p><em>Off Level 7 , combat and acuity alike.</em></p><h4>Skills</h4><table><tr><th>Thievery</th><th>Sailing Lore (sky)</th><th>Diplomacy</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+17</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+17</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>Moderate</td></tr></table><h4>Saves &amp; Perception</h4><table><tr><th>Fort</th><th>Reflex</th><th>Will</th><th>Perception</th></tr><tr><td><strong>+12</strong><br/>Low</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td><td><strong>+15</strong><br/>Moderate</td><td><strong>+18</strong><br/>High</td></tr></table><h4>DCs to act on her</h4><table><tr><th>Will DC</th><th>Perception DC</th></tr><tr><td><strong>25</strong><br/>coerce · demoralise · impress · talk her down</td><td><strong>28</strong><br/>lie · steal · sneak</td></tr></table><p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Ratfolk · 24</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Newly elected captain of the keepers, the crews of Goldwake's other two airships</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>Level 7 · Non-Combat Level 7</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Small and quick, sleek brown fur, whiskers trimmed neat for the occasion, a notch in one ear and bright black eyes that never stop moving. Thin; the keepers eat poorly.</p><p><strong>Dress: </strong>A captain's coat two sizes too grand, out of a keepers' chest, the cuffs rolled twice; underneath, patched sky-crew canvas. A ring of keys she has not yet got used to.</p><p><strong>Voice: </strong>Fast and sure; says \"ours\" a lot.</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"There's a ship under the Jigger nobody has boarded in a hundred and forty years. She's ours by right.\"</p><p><strong>Mannerisms: </strong>Touches the keys; finishes other people's sentences; looks at the Unspent every time she passes a rail.</p><p><strong>Disposition: </strong>Friendly (she needs them)</p><p><strong>Goal: </strong>Open the Unspent, sell what is inside, and pay the keepers what Goldwake never did.</p><p><strong>Background: </strong>A grandchild of Goldwake's veterans. Voted in at the last count of hands on the promise to open the ship. Opens the cabin door herself if the party hesitates.</p><p><strong>Faith: </strong>Fisaya, like the sky crews</p><p><strong>Faction &amp; ties: </strong>The keepers · Nirfel (whose whisper she takes for her own conviction)</p><p><strong>Fear: </strong>Being the captain who failed them</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Alive</p><section class=\"secret\"><p><strong>⚿ Secret</strong></p><p>She hears \"yours by right\" in her sleep, and thinks it is her own voice.</p></section>"}, {"name": "Mara Goldwake", "type": "text", "html": "<p><img src=\"worlds/heavens-dragons/assets/the-unspent/mara-goldwake.webp\" width=\"320\"></p>\n<p><em>Aboard the Unspent</em></p>\n<p><strong>The dead Lord · now Nirfel · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<p><em>Even dead, she looks like she is counting.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Tengu · died at about seventy, c. 2390 MR</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>A Pirate Lord of the sky; her body sits in her cabin</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>None (a body)</p><p><strong>Looks: </strong>Black feathers dulled with a century and a half of dust and a salt tarnish, small rings on her beak, each marked for something only she knew. Her coat is buttoned, every button a different metal. Talons in ship-leather boots. One hand closed around the glowing lift-heart.</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>Dead; her soul is Nirfel in Bolverk</p>"}, {"name": "Nirfel", "type": "text", "html": "<p><em>Aboard the Unspent</em></p>\n<p><strong>The whisper · Greed · Cardboard</strong></p>\n<p><em>A voice like coins sliding through fingers.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Pronouns: </strong>she/her</p><p><strong>Ancestry · age: </strong>Vice Demon of Greed (Goldwake's soul)</p><p><strong>Occupation: </strong>Whispers to the deserving-feeling</p><p><strong>Level: </strong>None at the table: a voice</p><p><strong>Sample line: </strong>\"It is not anyone else's. It is yours by right.\"</p><p><strong>Status: </strong>In Bolverk; acts only by whisper. Taking from her cache leaves the Greed-mark.</p>"}]}]};
  let folder = game.folders.find(f => f.type === "JournalEntry" && f.name === SPEC.folder && !f.folder);
  if (!folder) folder = await Folder.create({ name: SPEC.folder, type: "JournalEntry" });
  const made = [], replaced = [];
  for (const j of SPEC.journals) {
    const old = game.journal.find(e => e.folder?.id === folder.id && e.name === j.name);
    if (old) { await old.delete(); replaced.push(j.name); }
    const pages = j.pages.map((p, i) => p.type === "image"
      ? { name: p.name, type: "image", src: p.src, image: { caption: p.caption || "" }, sort: (i + 1) * 1000 }
      : { name: p.name, type: "text", text: { content: p.html, format: 1 }, sort: (i + 1) * 1000 });
    await JournalEntry.create({ name: j.name, folder: folder.id, pages });
    made.push(`${j.name} (${pages.length} pages)`);
  }
  await ChatMessage.create({ content: `<h3>Journals in ${SPEC.folder}</h3><ul>${made.map(x => "<li>" + x + "</li>").join("")}</ul>` +
    (replaced.length ? `<p><i>Replaced: ${replaced.join(", ")}</i></p>` : ""), whisper: [game.user.id] });
  ui.notifications.info(`Built ${made.length} journal(s) in ${SPEC.folder}.`);
})();
